NO SCOPE NARROWING: the manifest record extracted 0 named panels/charts for this unit, but the web
source has many regions. Every one was reproduced natively (not stubbed): the 6 summary stat cards,
the monthly-cost area chart, the cost-per-kWh line chart, the charger-type pie + breakdown bars, the
gas-vs-EV savings calculator (3 editable inputs + 4 comparison tiles + reset), the sortable monthly
cost table, the time-of-use hourly bar chart + 4 insight tiles, the opt-in AI-narration slot (web
`AICostForecastNarration` position; baseline injects EmptyView, mirroring TrueCost), the server
cost-forecast section (forecast composed chart + breakdown donut + savings panel + insights list +
cost-per-kWh trend), the lifetime summary (7 tiles) and the environmental-impact panel. Each region
renders its own loading/empty/success state — never a blank panel.

Data sources (web parity; web hook names kept at the Swift call sites per the manifest):
  useChargingSessionsPaginated -> CostAnalysisDataSource.loadChargingSessionsPaginated(vehicleID:)
                                  (GET /charging?vehicle_id&limit=5000&start&end)
  useCostForecast              -> CostAnalysisDataSource.loadCostForecast(vehicleID:)
                                  (GET /analytics/cost-forecast?vehicle_id&months)
  (The forecast TYPE was namespaced CostForecast->CostAnalysisForecast to avoid a symbol clash with
   the existing TeslaSync/feature-views/CostForecastSection + ForecastDetails parity artifacts; the
   loadCostForecast method + useCostForecast hook reference keep the web name.)

SI discipline (ADR-005, SI-cutover instructions): sessions carry the Phase-42 SI columns verbatim —
energy in watt-hours, power in watts, odometer in meters — and money is a currency amount. Energy
economics use kWh = Wh/1000 (the exact unit the web `convertEnergyFromSI(wh,'kWh')` applies) and the
gallon/MPG math is intrinsically in miles, so neither depends on the display preference. The distance
the user SEES (cost-per-distance card + the calculator per-distance chips) converts to their unit only
at the SwiftUI render boundary via the shared KMP `Units` facade (`CostAnalysisFormat`); nothing
non-SI is stored or computed in the model.

